[00:09.50] I'm watching the clock tick the hours away
[00:16.78] They say that I must hang at the dawn of the day
[00:25.36] But why should I fear death for it's life anew
[00:33.80] For dying only takes me much nearer to you
[00:40.96] You left me in anger to walk by the sea
[00:49.68] And when they found your body they blamed it on me
[00:57.70] But you know they were wrong dear so wait for awhile
[01:06.04] For we shall be together beyond the last mile
[01:14.18] [ Fiddle ]
[01:46.46] The stars hide their face to make way for the sun
[01:53.54] And soon death it shall claim me and make us as one
[02:01.92] While others are walking the streets with a smile
[02:10.20] Then I know I'll be walking beyond the last mile
[02:17.70] The chaplain is making his last plea to God
[02:25.96] Soon up the numbered steps to the scaffold I'll trod
[02:34.48] My footsteps won't falter I'll walk with a smile
[02:42.54] For I know you'll be waiting beyond the last mile
